  id: Buccal_part_of_buccinator_muscle.L
  partName: Buccal part of buccinator muscle L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'This muscle forms the muscular base of the cheek and plays a crucial role in
    mastication by compressing the cheek against the teeth. It prevents food from
    collecting between the teeth and cheeks, ensuring efficient chewing. '
  - It also assists in actions such as blowing, sucking, and whistling by maintaining
    intraoral pressure. Additionally, it works in coordination with the lips and
    tongue to control facial expressions and speech, contributing to overall oral
    function and fine motor control.
